{#
  ============================================================================
  radcli-redhat: RADIUS Dictionary Translation File
  ============================================================================
  
  This template generates the RADIUS attribute dictionary used by
  radcli (RADIUS client utilities) to parse Attribute/Value Pairs.
  
  The file defines standard RADIUS attributes (RFC 2865, RFC 2866, etc.)
  and their data types (string, integer, ipv4addr, ipv6addr, ipv6prefix, date).
  
  Variables are NOT used in this template because the schema provided is
  empty. The dictionary is a static, canonical definition required by
  the radcli library. It does not depend on dynamic configuration or
  external service connections.
  #}

#
# Updated 97/06/13 to livingston-radius-2.01 miquels@cistron.nl
#
#	This file contains dictionary translations for parsing
#	requests and generating responses.  All transactions are
#	composed of Attribute/Value Pairs.  The value of each attribute
#	is specified as one of 4 data types.  Valid data types are:
#
#	string - 0-253 octets
#	ipv4addr- 4 octets in network byte order
#	ipv6addr  - 16 octets in network byte order
#	ipv6prefix- up to 16 octets in network byte order, plus prefix length
#	integer - 32 bit value in big endian order (high byte first)
#	date - 32 bit value in big endian order - seconds since
#					00:00:00 GMT,  Jan.  1,  1970
#
#	Enumerated values are stored in the user file with dictionary
#	VALUE translations for easy administration.
#
#	Example:
#
#	ATTRIBUTE	  VALUE
#	---------------   -----
#	Framed-Protocol = PPP
#	7		= 1	(integer encoding)
#

#
#	Following are the proper new names. Use these.
#

# Standard RADIUS Attributes (RFC 2865)
# User-Name: Unique name of the user requesting access
ATTRIBUTE	User-Name		1	string
# Password: Used for PAP authentication; encrypted in transit
ATTRIBUTE	Password		2	string
# CHAP-Password: CHAP challenge-response value
ATTRIBUTE	CHAP-Password		3	string
# NAS-IP-Address: IP address of the Network Access Server
ATTRIBUTE	NAS-IP-Address		4	ipv4addr
# NAS-Port-Id: Logical port of the NAS
ATTRIBUTE	NAS-Port-Id		5	integer
# Service-Type: Determines the service the user requests
ATTRIBUTE	Service-Type		6	integer
# Framed-Protocol: Protocol for framed connections (PPP, SLIP)
ATTRIBUTE	Framed-Protocol		7	integer
# Framed-IP-Address: IP address assigned to the user
ATTRIBUTE	Framed-IP-Address	8	ipv4addr
# Framed-IP-Netmask: Subnet mask for the framed IP
ATTRIBUTE	Framed-IP-Netmask	9	ipv4addr
# Framed-Routing: Routing instruction (None, Broadcast, Listen)
ATTRIBUTE	Framed-Routing		10	integer
# Filter-Id: Pre-defined filter to apply
ATTRIBUTE	Filter-Id		11	string
# Framed-MTU: Maximum Transmission Unit for the session
ATTRIBUTE	Framed-MTU		12	integer
# Framed-Compression: Compression protocol requested
ATTRIBUTE	Framed-Compression	13	integer
# Login-IP-Host: IP host for login (historical)
ATTRIBUTE	Login-IP-Host		14	ipv4addr
# Login-Service: Service type for login (Telnet, Rlogin)
ATTRIBUTE	Login-Service		15	integer
# Login-TCP-Port: TCP port for login
ATTRIBUTE	Login-TCP-Port		16	integer
# Reply-Message: Text message to send to the client
ATTRIBUTE	Reply-Message		18	string
# Callback-Number: Number to call back
ATTRIBUTE	Callback-Number		19	string
# Callback-Id: Additional ID for callback
ATTRIBUTE	Callback-Id		20	string
# Framed-Route: Static route to add to the client
ATTRIBUTE	Framed-Route		22	string
# Framed-IPX-Network: IPX network number
ATTRIBUTE	Framed-IPX-Network	23	ipv4addr
# State: State of the session
ATTRIBUTE	State			24	string
# Class: Shared secret class
ATTRIBUTE	Class			25	string
# Vendor-Specific: Vendor-specific information
ATTRIBUTE	Vendor-Specific		26	string
# Session-Timeout: Maximum seconds for the session
ATTRIBUTE	Session-Timeout		27	integer
# Idle-Timeout: Maximum idle seconds before disconnect
ATTRIBUTE	Idle-Timeout		28	integer
# Termination-Action: Action upon session termination
ATTRIBUTE	Termination-Action	29	integer
# Called-Station-Id: Number of the called station
ATTRIBUTE	Called-Station-Id	30	string
# Calling-Station-Id: Number of the calling station
ATTRIBUTE	Calling-Station-Id	31	string
# NAS-Identifier: Identifier for the NAS
ATTRIBUTE	NAS-Identifier		32	string
# Proxy-State: State information passed in proxy requests
ATTRIBUTE	Proxy-State		33	string
# Login-LAT-Service: LAT service for login
ATTRIBUTE	Login-LAT-Service	34	string
# Login-LAT-Node: LAT node for login
ATTRIBUTE	Login-LAT-Node		35	string
# Login-LAT-Group: LAT group for login
ATTRIBUTE	Login-LAT-Group		36	string
# Framed-AppleTalk-Link: AppleTalk link
ATTRIBUTE	Framed-AppleTalk-Link	37	integer
# Framed-AppleTalk-Network: AppleTalk network
ATTRIBUTE	Framed-AppleTalk-Network	38	integer
# Framed-AppleTalk-Zone: AppleTalk zone
ATTRIBUTE	Framed-AppleTalk-Zone	39	string
# Acct-Status-Type: Accounting status (Start, Stop, Alive)
ATTRIBUTE	Acct-Status-Type	40	integer
# Acct-Delay-Time: Time accounting records were delayed
ATTRIBUTE	Acct-Delay-Time		41	integer
# Acct-Input-Octets: Total octets received during session
ATTRIBUTE	Acct-Input-Octets	42	integer
# Acct-Output-Octets: Total octets sent during session
ATTRIBUTE	Acct-Output-Octets	43	integer
# Acct-Session-Id: Unique session ID for accounting
ATTRIBUTE	Acct-Session-Id		44	string
# Acct-Authentic: Authentication type used
ATTRIBUTE	Acct-Authentic		45	integer
# Acct-Session-Time: Total seconds of session
ATTRIBUTE	Acct-Session-Time	46	integer
# Acct-Input-Packets: Total packets received
ATTRIBUTE	Acct-Input-Packets	47	integer
# Acct-Output-Packets: Total packets sent
ATTRIBUTE	Acct-Output-Packets	48	integer
# Acct-Terminate-Cause: Reason for session termination
ATTRIBUTE	Acct-Terminate-Cause	49	integer
# Acct-Multi-Session-Id: ID for multi-session accounting
